.Dd October 21, 2026
.Dt MIDNIGHTBSD-CHAT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm midnightbsd-chat
.Nd local AI chat companion for Midnight Workspace
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
provides saved conversations with an OpenAI-compatible chat endpoint.
Select a saved server using the Server dropdown. Add server creates a named
profile; Settings edits the selected profile, and Remove server deletes it
after confirmation. Keep between 1 and 32 profiles. Each profile remembers its
endpoint, optional bearer token, model, context and reply limits, request
deadline, and tool settings. New profiles have authentication and tools disabled.
Existing single-server settings migrate to the first profile on the next save.
Switching preserves the current conversation and draft; subsequent requests
send that conversation's context to the selected server. Switching is disabled
while a request runs. Removing a server does not delete conversations.
Choose Settings to configure an HTTP or HTTPS base URL, port, optional bearer
token, and context and reply token limits.
The default endpoint is http://localhost/v1 on port 11434 (Ollama).
For llama.cpp use port 8080.
Port zero preserves the URL port or the scheme default.
Use Refresh models to populate the editable model dropdown from /v1/models.
The base path defaults to /v1; /chat/completions is appended for chat requests.
.Pp
Select conversations on the left or create a new conversation.
Control+Enter sends a message; Enter inserts a newline.
Stop cancels a request. Send / Retry retries an unanswered message;
entering replacement text edits that pending message.
Only one request runs at a time; conversations can be viewed while waiting.
.Pp
Older complete turns are summarized automatically through the same endpoint
when the conservative byte-based token estimate exceeds the context budget.
Reply space and template overhead are reserved. The complete transcript is
retained locally. Summaries can lose details. Reset context excludes earlier
turns from future requests without deleting them from the transcript.
Set the context size to the server's actual configured capacity.
This setting does not reconfigure the server.
.Pp
Responses are displayed as plain text after generation completes.
The Tools settings tab optionally enables filename search, system information,
read-only mport package queries, and web search. All tools are disabled by default.
A tool-capable model is required when enabled. File search returns readable
indexed paths without reading contents. Package queries use the installed
registry or cached index without updating either. A dedicated count tool returns
the exact total; searches report exact totals before their limited previews.
Search text is literal, not a wildcard. Web search supports Brave
with an API key, or a configured SearXNG JSON search URL.
.Pp
Local tool results are sent to the configured model server. Web queries go to
the selected search provider. Calls and result previews are saved in the
transcript. Replies default to 12 rounds and 24 calls. Settings / Tools allows
1–32 rounds and 1–64 calls per reply. Repeated identical searches refer to earlier
results without executing again, and still count toward the limits.
Settings / Connection sets a request deadline of 60–3600 seconds (default 900),
including model exchanges and compaction.
At the limit, the model is asked to state findings and unresolved questions
from collected results with tools disabled.
Further tool requests are ignored; collected results are preserved with a notice
if the model provides no final answer.
Output is
bounded and explicitly truncated when needed to fit context. Stop also cancels
tools. The application cannot execute arbitrary model-generated commands or
install or remove packages.
TLS certificates are verified, redirects are rejected, and environment proxies
are not used. Authentication is omitted unless explicitly enabled.
Tokens are stored in a private file, not encrypted; use HTTPS when appropriate.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/midnightbsd-chat/settings.json
Endpoint, model, authentication and token limits (mode 0600).
.It Pa $XDG_DATA_HOME/midnightbsd-chat/conversations.json
Conversation transcripts and summaries (mode 0600).
.El
.Pp
XDG defaults are ~/.config and ~/.local/share.
Invalid or insecure files are reported and preserved, not overwritten.
History is limited to 16 MiB and 1000 conversations; delete older conversations
when the limit is reached. Responses are limited to 1 MiB.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr midnight-wm 1 ,
.Xr midnightbsd-search 1
